(*
porta space-sync — THE KERNEL OWNS THE BASE TICK (rete#231 D1).

Why the kernel and not each app, and why nsl and not C: a heartbeat a wedged node
can still emit is a lie — it is `port=up` exactly, which is the failure #152 is
about. So the tick rides the reactor. It also costs NO new C: `timer_target_snapshot`
already reports every live repeating timer to #215's observer, so one kernel-owned
`timers every:` gives the detector a deadline that always exists AND drives the
check-in. A node whose app declares no timer at all stops being invisible.

THE BRIDGE IS HANDED THE APP'S ONE `timers`, never mints its own: `platform timers`
answers a FRESH instance every send and the C timer registry is keyed globally, so
two instances alias each other's tokens and misfire silently. `pendingCount` on the
instance the APP holds is what proves the bridge used that one.

ONCE. A second startTicking: must not register a second timer — two timers at the
same period is two check-ins per tick forever, and the second one is invisible until
someone counts radio wakeups.

expect:
before 0
after 1
handed instance 1
idempotent 1
*)
class KernelTick packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space timers bridge tickChan |
    space:: platform space.
    timers:: platform timers.
    tickChan:: space channel: 'sys/tick'.
    bridge:: platform PortaBridge socket: nil space: space id: 'test' peer: '::1' port: 1
      spans: platform Spans new.
    bridge liveness: 2000 misses: 8.

    ('before ' , timers pendingCount printString) println.
    bridge startTicking: timers on: tickChan.
    ('after ' , timers pendingCount printString) println.

    (* The registration landed on the instance the APP holds, which is the whole
       point: a bridge that sent `platform timers` for itself would leave this at
       0 and dispatch would silently drop every tick. *)
    ('handed instance ' , timers pendingCount printString) println.

    bridge startTicking: timers on: tickChan.
    ('idempotent ' , timers pendingCount printString) println.
  )
) : (
)
